d6cbbf747fdf9cbdf3579b0e6f4"], "tags": []}], "date": 1791983509, "git_changesets": ["b66feef7e3c153f062d9a27e675e5c8f8cc1aed0"], "user": "ffxbld@lando.moz.tools"}, "28921": {"changesets": [{"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2081740 - Run repo-update-pinning-update on b-linux workers. r=releng-reviewers,jcristau a=NPOTB DONTBUILD\n\nb-linux-medium also schedules workers in northamerica-northeast1, where the task currently times out. b-linux\nonly uses us-central1 and us-west1.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333631\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/repo-update/kind.yml"], "git_node": "9be801ee5c170a1160f12680afaaaed4ab6e5c86", "git_parents": ["e58a0ee7d9764a9b881c299ffcc18b38e063078c"], "node": "88c614ddeb9d4ae8ee5621aea92314c98b3573e4", "parents": ["1b1fcf3923fb8a4f24367c02ae63891416a90e75"], "tags": []}], "date": 1791983627, "git_changesets": ["9be801ee5c170a1160f12680afaaaed4ab6e5c86"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "28922": {"changesets": [{"author": "Release Engineering Landoscript \u003crelease+landoscript@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Automatic version bump NO BUG a=release CLOSED TREE DONTBUILD\n", "files": ["browser/config/version_display.txt", "mobile/android/version.txt"], "git_node": "0044a93d83959ef4de06c438e6a5931ce9285b0b", "git_parents": ["9be801ee5c170a1160f12680afaaaed4ab6e5c86"], "node": "52b66935d2e0b002a1a57a8d55a8b8884c352b4c", "parents": ["88c614ddeb9d4ae8ee5621aea92314c98b3573e4"], "tags": []}], "date": 1791984879, "git_changesets": ["0044a93d83959ef4de06c438e6a5931ce9285b0b"], "user": "ffxbld@lando.moz.tools"}, "28923": {"changesets": [{"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@lando.moz.tools\u003e", "branch": "tags-unified", "desc": "No bug - Tagging fc7b5f0153f851eecfbdd5567e5f1de8bb3a0584 with FIREFOX-ANDROID_159_0b2_RELEASE a=tagging CLOSED TREE DONTBUILD", "files": [".hgtags"], "git_node": "78aeecafb3fdf0079b0b8f67359c4da3ab2272f1", "git_parents": ["b66feef7e3c153f062d9a27e675e5c8f8cc1aed0"], "node": "0dee593e7e121ea3a83768625a51849f3b4370c8", "parents": ["199fb22c8a3c1aa493a6b0348f277aa487d5be69"], "tags": []}], "date": 1791984897, "git_changesets": ["78aeecafb3fdf0079b0b8f67359c4da3ab2272f1"], "user": "ffxbld@lando.moz.tools"}, "28924": {"changesets": [{"author": "Jari Jalkanen \u003cjjalkanen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069097: Fix excess dirty-origin writes at startup.  a=RyanVM\n\nAfter a build-ID change, dirty shutdown, or migration, scanned origin\nmetadata often has a stale mLastAccessTime from .metadata-v2 that\ndiffers from the DB row. This caused cacheRowMatches=false and an\nunnecessary dirty-queue push for origins whose usage was otherwise\nidentical.\n\nReconcile timestamps before comparing, replace the mOriginUsage\u003e0\nguard with aDirectoryExists, add an mUsageModificationDisabled guard,\nand re-enable that flag after RemoveQuota in the full-scan path.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327351\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333537\n", "files": ["dom/quota/ActorsParent.cpp", "dom/quota/CommonMetadata.h", "dom/quota/test/xpcshell/test_unaccessedOrigins.js"], "git_node": "e7862a1ead8a485831dfee85659fbb47a466a2a5", "git_parents": ["0044a93d83959ef4de06c438e6a5931ce9285b0b"], "node": "d805c82354b525e60e5b8165ddc4aed403a76ad2", "parents": ["52b66935d2e0b002a1a57a8d55a8b8884c352b4c"], "tags": []}], "date": 1791991845, "git_changesets": ["e7862a1ead8a485831dfee85659fbb47a466a2a5"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "28925": {"changesets": [{"author": "Nicolas Silva \u003cnsilva@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2079984 - Round up nine-patch segment render task size.  a=RyanVM\n\nThe device-space size of a nine-patch segment can be fractional where the\nsegment intersects the antialiased bounds of the primitive, and truncating\nit to an integer can produce an empty render task. Round the size up so\nthat the task is never empty and still covers the area that gets drawn.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332390\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333550\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/quad.rs", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/clip/reftest.list", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/clip/rounded-clip-subpixel-corner.yaml"], "git_node": "052472e1423b6704e3ac4538d764735e13e822ed", "git_parents": ["e7862a1ead8a485831dfee85659fbb47a466a2a5"], "node": "a8920d12012146eec12f10139167210821c3ae71", "parents": ["d805c82354b525e60e5b8165ddc4aed403a76ad2"], "tags": []}], "date": 1791991871, "git_changesets": ["052472e1423b6704e3ac4538d764735e13e822ed"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "28926": {"changesets": [{"author": "James Teh \u003cjteh@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2078941: Don't bother looking up PDF ids when it isn't useful.  a=RyanVM\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D331485\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333510\n", "files": ["accessible/pdf/PdfStructTreeBuilder.cpp"], "git_node": "3765427518e2a7e47074497e467abd1f056908f5", "git_parents": ["052472e1423b6704e3ac4538d764735e13e822ed"], "node": "89571c4e7da891ff3f37878a3640a95f02fbffc2", "parents": ["a8920d12012146eec12f10139167210821c3ae71"], "tags": []}], "date": 1791991903, "git_changesets": ["3765427518e2a7e47074497e467abd1f056908f5"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "28927": {"changesets": [{"author": "Jon Coppeard \u003cjcoppeard@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073936 - Fix post barrier in buffer allocator test code  a=RyanVM\n\nThe buffer allocator jsapi tests want to allocate a bunch of nursery-owned\nbuffers without also having to allocate nursery objects to hold them. To do\nthis we add the (tenured) holder object to the whole cell store buffer so that\nit gets traced on minor GC. This ends up tracing the buffers as if they had\nbeen referenced from some traced nursery object. However we don't trace the\nstore buffers if the nursery is empty so this can fail.\n\nThe patch ensures the nursery is not empty when adding these store buffer\nentries.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332852\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333546\n", "files": ["js/src/jsapi-tests/testGCAllocator.cpp"], "git_node": "3341203af18a6e5a9e57536c1b7a5c9566dd29bd", "git_parents": ["3765427518e2a7e47074497e467abd1f056908f5"], "node": "8897ecd9754d96101128744e505836a43acdfbf7", "parents": ["89571c4e7da891ff3f37878a3640a95f02fbffc2"], "tags": []}], "date": 1791991937, "git_changesets": ["3341203af18a6e5a9e57536c1b7a5c9566dd29bd"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "28928": {"changesets": [{"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080641 - More consistently deal with FontFaceSet promise resolution.  a=RyanVM\n\nDon't use the ready promise status as a proxy for \"do we need to\nschedule the resolve\".\n\nThis prevents .ready from resolving when other loads have started after\nthe fact already.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332819\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333530\n", "files": ["layout/style/FontFaceImpl.cpp", "layout/style/FontFaceSet.cpp", "layout/style/FontFaceSet.h", "layout/style/FontFaceSetDocumentImpl.cpp", "layout/style/FontFaceSetImpl.cpp", "layout/style/FontFaceSetImpl.h"], "git_node": "880d9124dc9c011ce3e4ec4c01ef92393f7791d2", "git_parents": ["3341203af18a6e5a9e57536c1b7a5c9566dd29bd"], "node": "868b88558a12464e4aac5e9a5056875388958b53", "parents": ["8897ecd9754d96101128744e505836a43acdfbf7"], "tags": []}], "date": 1791991970, "git_changesets": ["880d9124dc9c011ce3e4ec4c01ef92393f7791d2"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "28929": {"changesets": [{"author": "Iain Ireland \u003ciireland@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075990: Make typed loads non-movable  a=RyanVM\n\nTyped loads are used in self-hosted code to access reserved slots. In cases where the contents of a reserved slot depend on control flow, we want to ensure that the load isn't hoisted above the code that guards it.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332615\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333713\n", "files": ["js/src/jit-test/tests/regexp/bug2075990.js", "js/src/jit/WarpCacheIRTranspiler.cpp"], "git_node": "ad6813dc493bb696e770bb561b59909c9332123b", "git_parents": ["880d9124dc9c011ce3e4ec4c01ef92393f7791d2"], "node": "7c298acef987db922aa928fd49de7a53aef93d54", "parents": ["868b88558a12464e4aac5e9a5056875388958b53"], "tags": []}], "date": 1791992007, "git_changesets": ["ad6813dc493bb696e770bb561b59909c9332123b"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "28930": {"changesets": [{"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2081030 - Annotate fontface-descriptor-updates as passing everywhere. a=test-only DONTBUILD\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-font-loading/fontface-descriptor-updates.html.ini"], "git_node": "13a0d0ee6df3a4058311ab6a38833839ff868f71", "git_parents": ["ad6813dc493bb696e770bb561b59909c9332123b"], "node": "18f3518805fadade7fe1c3c75e2a0cad155d7e5e", "parents": ["7c298acef987db922aa928fd49de7a53aef93d54"], "tags": []}], "date": 1791993193, "git_changesets": ["13a0d0ee6df3a4058311ab6a38833839ff868f71"], "user": "rvandermeulen@mozilla.com"}, "28931": {"changesets": [{"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080975 - Keep failures of tests that will be retried as FAIL in resource usage profile markers.  a=RyanVM DONTBUILD\n\nThe harnesses make expected match status when a test will be retried, so the\nfailure arrived looking like a todo() and became KNOWN-